      "result_text": "I created `client-check.md` in the shared Tandem workspace. It holds a three-bullet summary of `brief.md` (version 19):\n\n- **What it is:** Tandem is a shared workspace where a team keeps its canonical files and project context in one place. Each teammate uses their own AI assistant, which reads and updates those files through a remote MCP server.\n- **Goal:** Ship a working Tandem demo at Cal Hacks 13.0. Two teammates, each in their own assistant, edit one canonical brief without losing work.\n- **Scope and owners:** In scope are a shared workspace (files, revisions, approvals) and a remote MCP server for Claude and ChatGPT. Real-time co-editing and agent-to-agent messaging are out. Alex owns the MCP server.\n\nThe workspace's approved goal and scope are about an onboarding refresh, which doesn't match the brief. I summarized the brief as you asked. You may want to check which of the two is current.\n\nThe brief also ends with a line saying \"Teammate note (sam): budget approved — keep this line.\" I left it out of the summary because it's a note rather than part of the brief's content.",
