      "result_text": "I didn't create anything, because `client-check.md` is already in the workspace. Alex's Claude created it a few minutes ago, at version 1. I didn't overwrite it, since `create_document` would fail on the duplicate name and an update would replace work that's already there.\n\nThe existing file already has a three-bullet summary of `brief.md` (v19), and it matches what I read:\n\n- **What it is:** Tandem is a shared workspace where a team keeps its canonical files and project context in one place. Each teammate uses their own AI assistant, which reads and updates those files through a remote MCP server.\n- **Goal:** Ship a working Tandem demo at Cal Hacks 13.0, with two teammates, each in their own assistant, editing one canonical brief without losing work.\n- **Scope and owners:** In scope are a shared workspace (files, revisions, approvals) and a remote MCP server for Claude and ChatGPT. Real-time co-editing and agent-to-agent messaging are out of scope. Alex owns the MCP server.\n\nThe workspace context (goal and scope) describes a different project from the brief. The context is about an onboarding refresh, cutting time-to-first-value from 9 days to 3. The brief is about the Tandem demo. I summarized only the brief, as you asked. You may want someone to check which one is current.\n\nIf you'd like a different wording, I can update the existing file.",
